As per IDF query semantics, if there is an attribute that is an entity type name, we consider that as an ancestor relation in the relationship graph.
For instance:
query {
entity_list {
entity_type_name: "alert"
}
..
group_by {
group_by_column : “cluster”
…
}
}
Here, the client has requested alert entities from IDF, and wants the entities to be grouped on cluster. As per the current query implementation:
we traverse the relationship graph.
for each alert, we create buckets based on the values of “cluster” (result of relationship walk).
Add the entities to the corresponding buckets.
