[IDF Design Documents | Backup of Namespaces]
## Problem Statement
IDF backs up entities created locally on PC to the configured backup endpoints (registered PEs and S3 compatible storage) seamlessly but current offering does not backup the Namespaces added on top of replicated entities.
Multiple components are planning to use Namespaces on top of replicated entities for performance and clean design on PC. Since most of these use-cases plan to add data provided by end-users like Categories, rules, etc as a Namespace on top of replicated entities, this data needs to be backed up and recovered on PC-restore.

## Schema Changes to configure Backup of Namespaces
Currently, there is no separate registration required for Namespaces but for enabling backup we will have to allow Namespace registration via schema files and RPCs in IDF.
Sample namespace schema will look like:-
entity_type_info_list {
entity_type_name: "namespace_etype"
type_info {
namespace_list {
namespace: "namespace_1"
backup_replication_control {
is_backup_required: true
}
}
}
}
Note:- For maintaining Backwards compatibility, we can not mandate registration of Namespaces for everyone. Namespace registration is only needed when Backup needs to be enabled at Namespace level. By default, a Namespace will not be backed-up if not explicitly mentioned in the schema.

[IDF Design Documents | PC DR V1 final implementation]
## Marking an entity type to be backed-up
While registering the entity type, users can provide information whether to backup the entities of this type or not.
Sample config example:-
entity_type_info_list {
entity_type_name : "tag"
type_info {
track_attribute_changes : false
backup_replication_control {
is_backup_required: true
}
...
}
}
Today, IDF only supports taking backup of entities created on PC so this flag will not have any effect on entities which are created on PE side.
As of now, IDF only supports Backup and Restore for entity types which are registered via config and not for the types which are registered dynamically (via RPC). This limitation exists because IDF sync do not auto register the entity types on the replica side so for dynamically registered entity types backup will go through but Restore will not happen, as the new PC will only have entity types which were registered in config and not the dynamic entity types (which might have been registered by various components in different workflows on the older PC).

