[IDF Design Documents | Multihop IDF Sync]
Sync-Barrier Timestamps When a synced entity arrives at an intermediate hop (e.g., ID), its sync-barrier timestamp must be restamped with the local hop’s barrier timestamp. This ensures downstream hops evaluate barrier ordering using the local hop’s perspective, maintaining strict ordering for both local and incoming entities. Extend Replication Control List (RCL) The current RCL schema supports only single-hop (source → destination) definitions. For multi-hop, clients must be able to specify the entire replication path, including all intermediate hops, in an ordered manner. A new schema (CascadingReplicationControl) needs to be introduced to model full replication chains like: PE → ID → PC ID → PC1 NOTE: Currently, Selective sync of entities is not supported in V1. We will discuss the design in the future version.

