[IDF Design Documents | [Won_t fix] Suppress the ActiveEntitiesInfo sync via sending unsupported entity type list]
## Main Code Changes
New field to RemoteTransferDataRet:
message RemoteTransferDataRet {
…
repeated string unsupported_entity_type_list = 3;
}
message LoadActiveEntitiesInfoArg {
…
repeated string unsupported_entity_type_list = 3;
}
In class InsightsUploader::Bootstrapper, instead of keeping only the endpoint_ids in the ‘endpoints_requested_active_entities_info_’, we need to also attach the unsupported list of this StreamKey on a particular endpoint. So the unsupported_entity_type_list is on the per stream per endpoint basis.
unordered_map<StreamKey, unordered_set<uint64 /* endpoint_ids */>> endpoints_requested_active_entities_info_;
->
unordered_map<StreamKey, unordered_map<uint64 /* endpoint_ids */, list<string/*unsupported_entity_type*/>>> endpoints_requested_active_entities_info_
The reason to track the unsupported entity type list on the basis of per endpoint is that different replicas can have different unsupported entity types. For example, entity type A exists in the master and replica X, but not in replica Y. Then this entity type will be non-evictable in Y (the IsEvictableEntityType() returns false).
In rpc and store layer, extend the LoadActiveEntitiesInfo to make use of the unsupported_entity_type_list to do the filtering.

