[IDF Documentation & Guides | IDF-IDF-sync-client]
a sync barrier update comes, we get the latest db modified timestamp of all the shards and store it in the sync_barrier_info of the entity object. When this sync barrier entity arrives on the replica side, we check if the fulfilled ranges for each shard have at least caught up to the timestamp value for each shard in sync_barrier_info. If this condition is satisfied, the entity gets replicated, else it is added to the sync barrier queue. Incase the sync barrier entity is queued, we issue long poll RPCs(NodeSyncBarrierWait) to each node to notify if all the shards owned by that node have caught up to the timestamp value of shard in sync_barrier_info. If the sync barrier condition is satisfied we replicate the entity, else we issue another set of long poll RPCs.

