[IDF Documentation & Guides | IDF Namespaces - V1]
## GetEntitiesWithMetrics support:
filter / sort / raw / aggregate / group-by columns need to be scoped by corresponding namespace name to fetch the sub-entity attributes. Cursor queries are supported.
Ancestor, Having Clause, Lookup queries on namespace attributes are not supported.
All the query features are disable for pseudo attributes belonging to namespaces.
For example:
select sum(N1::FOO), avg(N2::BAR)
group by N3::BAZ
where BAZ in ["a", "b", "c"]
In this example, FOO and BAR only exist in namespace N1 and N2, while BAZ exists in default and N3.
Following protos have been defined for query:
message LeafExpression {
optional string column_namespace = 3 [default = "_default_"];
}
message QueryGroupBy {
optional string group_by_column_namespace = 13 [default = "_default_"];
}
message QueryOrderBy {
optional string sort_column_namespace = 4 [default = "_default_"];
}
message QueryAggregateColumn {
optional string column_namespace = 4 [default = "_default_"];
}
message QueryRawColumn {
optional string column_namespace = 3 [default = "_default_"];
}
The namespace name will have to be populated in the required field to scope the relevant attributes to the desired namespace. For example, in order to retrieve all entities that have the namespace attribute ‘namespace_attr’ populated along with their corresponding attribute values. The query would look like:

