## Dynamic Registration
For the Dynamic Registration case we issue RegisterEntityType RPC which makes a fan out call to NodeRegisterEntityType RPC. We fetch the entity types to register from the InsightsUtil::GetRegisterEntityTypesInputFromArg method. Here unlike config based registration we do not compare the entity types from the config file with the entity types present in the cache. We then issue the PutEntityTypes method, to write the entity type definitions to Cassandra. Here there is a check to avoid redundant writes to Cassandra by checking if the same entity type definition is present in cache or not.
If the entity type definition has not changed, we exit early.
Same thing applies for metric types as well.

