periodic purging process, we have the following check to return early without purging: So for certain entities such as task entities which have direct_purge_on_replica_delete set to false and allow_entity_deletion_on_replica set to true, the replica deleted entities will not be purged unless the is_deleted_on_replica field is set to false by the ActiveEntities workflow. (This ensures that these entities get purged from replica only after they have been deleted from source). Since ActiveEntities workflow needs to check the entities on the replica side to compare them with entities present on the source side, it would not be able to find the replica deleted entities in Insights Cache. So here is where the replica_deleted_map would become useful. replica_deleted_map would have the necessary context stored for all the synced entities deleted on the replica and using that, it would scan those entities from Cassandra.

