[MongoDB Integration | IDF-Mongo Data Model]
## MongoDB Entity Collections Document Design
Entity proto buffer object will be translated directly to Mongo document, the translation is pretty straight forward with field_names and values being one-one mapping into the MongoDB BSON documents except for a few details:
BSON  (https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/bson-types/) does not support all the data types that are supported by the proto-buffer. We shall perform the data type translation for the non-repeated fields as following.
We shall convert the repeated field into BSON Array with values of the corresponding type of the element as described above.
BSON string type seems only support UTF encoded strings, we seem to have occasional cases where client encode the binary characters in the string, in those cases, we might need to store the field values in Binary Data in order to preserve the data.
IDF Entity proto-buffer message encodes the name value pairs as repeated field of the following message:
message NameTimeValuePair {
// Required.
optional string name = 1;
// Deprecated.
// optional TimeValuePair modified_time_value = 2;
// Required.
optional uint64 timestamp_usecs = 3;
// Required.
optional DataValue value = 4;
}

