## Query 2 ($exists)
Checking the existence / null cannot be fulfilled by examining the index alone.
db.students.explain("executionStats").aggregate([
{'$match': {'$or': [{'occupation_id': {'$in': []}},
{'occupation_id': {'$exists': false}}]}},
{'$project': {'occupation_id': 1, '_id': 0}},
{'$count': '_cnt_'}
])
Indexes:
occupation_id: a normal index
According to https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-18861, and https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-12869, MongoDB cannot distinguish null and non-existence in the index, and hence will always do a FETCH. Changing the filter to cover both cases as the following does not make much difference:
db.students.explain("executionStats").aggregate([
{'$match': {'$or': [{'occupation_id': {'$in': []}},
{'$or': [{'occupation_id': null},
{'occupation_id': {'$exists': false}}
]}
]}},
{'$count': '_cnt_'}
])

